# Every way of running Vine that docs/spec.md advertises, except the bare
# REPL, which has its own cases. Until this file existed the CLI was the one
# part of the project ./check never executed: the runner calls the library.
--version
-e 'print(1 + 1)'
tests/fixtures/greet.vine
tests/fixtures/broken.vine
-e 'print('
nosuchfile.vine
tests/fixtures/latin1.vine
-e

# A command line naming two programs. Vine ran the first and exited 0 on the
# rest until tick 9; these two are the shapes that reach it, a second file and
# a file beside -e.
tests/fixtures/greet.vine tests/fixtures/broken.vine
-e 'print(1)' tests/fixtures/greet.vine

# An argument that looks like an option and is not one. Vine has none past -e,
# -h and --version, so both of these are file names -- which the headline is
# true about and silent on, and which is what the help says.
--nope
-- tests/fixtures/greet.vine
